  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5256",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the pathogenesis of LB647-SCLC through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and a compound known as [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is both a target of doxorubicin and a potential mediator of its effects on LB647-SCLC cells. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin may act through a mechanism where it first targets P2X purinoceptor 1, which in turn is targeted by the compound. This creates a chain of interactions that ultimately leads to the activation of LB647-SCLC cells. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the same compound and its role as a target of doxorubicin supports the hypothesis that doxorubicin exerts its effects on LB647-SCLC through a complex, multi-step mechanism involving purinoceptor signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting this compound as a potential therapeutic strategy for the disease.",
